        "title": "fix(hooks): wire message:sending internal hook to user-defined hooks",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `message:sending` internal hook was registered but never invoked during outbound message delivery. Wires the hook into `deliver.ts` so user-defined hooks receive outgoing message events for logging, content filtering, or outbound audit purposes.\n\n## Linked context\n\nCloses #29365\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: `message:sending` hook never fired for outbound messages\n- Real environment tested: Local gateway with user-defined hook subscribing to `message:sending`\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n```\nvitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.hooks.config.ts \\\n    src/hooks/internal-hooks.test.ts\n\nvitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts \\\n    src/infra/outbound/deliver.test.ts\n```\n- Evidence after fix: 2 test files, 132 tests passed (vitest 4.1.8)\n- Observed result after fix: `message:sending` hook fires for every outbound message\n- What was not tested: Live Telegram/Matrix channel outbound delivery with mantis-proof screenshots\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: Hook delivery to real channels not tested in unit suite\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Commands: `vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.hooks.config.ts`, `vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts`\n- Regression coverage: internal-hooks.test.ts (36 tests), deliver.test.ts (96 tests)\n- Before: `message:sending` hook defined but call site missing in deliver.ts\n- After: Hook wired into outbound delivery path\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- Did user-visible behavior change? Yes — user-defined hooks now receive outbound message events\n- Did config, environment, or migration behavior change? No\n- Did security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? Yes — new hook invocation in delivery path\n- What is the highest-risk area? Message delivery: hook errors could interfere with outbound message sending\n- How is that risk mitigated? Hook failures are caught and logged; delivery proceeds regardless\n\n## Current review state\n\n- Next action: @clawsweeper re-review\n- Waiting on: ClawSweeper proof evaluation; mantis auto-generates Telegram-visible-proof",
